# tests/ci.env — self-hosted runner configuration for tests/report.sh (T2-T4).
# Copy to tests/ci.env (gitignored) on the runner and adjust the paths.
# Every value below shows its default; only K230_CI_WORKSPACE is required.

# Image tag the pipeline builds (stage 'image') and tests against.
#K230_CI_IMAGE=k230-builder:regression

# Persistent docker volume for toolchains + conan/NuGet caches.
# First run downloads ~5GB; afterwards toolchain stages are near-free.
# The per-run clean below never touches this volume, nor the conan/NuGet caches
# inside it: they are sha256-verified / content-addressed, and t2-toolchains.sh
# cross-compiles hello.c fresh every run anyway.
#K230_CI_VOLUME=k230_toolchains_ci

# Workspace root holding the SDK / nncase checkouts, laid out like the README
# recommends (t4 runtime builds mount THIS dir, so SDKs must live inside it):
#   $K230_CI_WORKSPACE/
#   ├── k230_linux_sdk/      built by stage sdk-linux, reused by nncase-runtime-linux
#   ├── k230_rtos_sdk/       built by stage sdk-rtos,  reused by nncase-runtime-rtos
#   ├── k230_nuttx_sdk/      west workspace, built by stage sdk-nuttx
#   ├── nncase/              base repo (auto-cloned by scripts/nncase if missing)
#   └── nncase-k80/          plugin repo — REQUIRED for the nncase-* stages
K230_CI_WORKSPACE=$HOME/k230-ci

# SDK dir names under the workspace (or absolute paths) and build commands.
# Each K230_CI_<X>_CMD runs as `k230 bash -c "$CMD"` — it can be a full shell
# sequence ("make list-def && make CONF=... && make", "a && b; c"), not just
# a single command.
# The Linux SDK's default full build is heavy (kernel + full rootfs + apps).
# If your k230_linux_sdk checkout supports a smaller/faster target (e.g. a
# leaner defconfig, or a single-component target like "make uboot"/"make
# linux"), point K230_CI_LINUX_CMD at that instead of the full image build —
# t3-sdk.sh only asserts a fresh matching K230_CI_LINUX_ART artifact, so pair a
# narrower command with a narrower _ART glob AND a matching _CLEAN_CMD — the
# post-clean zero-artifact check below compares the two.
#K230_CI_LINUX_SDK=k230_linux_sdk
#K230_CI_LINUX_CMD="make CONF=k230_canmv_defconfig"
#K230_CI_RTOS_SDK=k230_rtos_sdk
#K230_CI_RTOS_CMD="make CONF=k230_canmv_defconfig"
#K230_CI_NUTTX_SDK=k230_nuttx_sdk
#K230_CI_NUTTX_CMD="west build"

# Clean command run before EVERY SDK build, as `k230 bash -c "$CLEAN_CMD"` from
# the SDK dir — same container, same paths, same mechanism as the build.
# Every regression run is a full from-scratch build: the SDK checkouts persist
# across runs, so without a clean the build is an incremental no-op that compiles
# nothing and the stage passes vacuously. After cleaning and before building,
# t3-sdk.sh asserts the artifact glob matches ZERO files — a clean command that
# misses the build output FAILs the stage loudly instead of silently degrading
# back to a no-op.
#
# A clean is almost entirely a CPU cost, not a bandwidth one — the big download
# caches all sit outside the cleaned dirs (nuttx is the one exception, see below):
#   linux: output/ holds both the build AND the extracted buildroot, but dl/
#          (1.1GB, the buildroot tarball included) is its SIBLING and survives.
#          `make CONF=...` re-extracts and re-configures from dl/ for free.
#   rtos : sources live in src/ + .repo, toolchains in ~/.kendryte.
#          `rm -rf output` ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH — rtsmart/uboot/opensbi/canmv
#          build in-tree and leave hundreds of .o files under src/, so the
#          default runs `make clean` first (it delegates to each component's
#          kbuild clean) and only then removes output/. Do NOT "upgrade" this to
#          `make distclean`: that deletes .config, and the default build command
#          `make CONF=...` is not a %_defconfig goal, so the next build dies with
#          "Please run make xxx_defconfig first".
#   nuttx: `west clean` removes build/, output/ and the top-level *.img, and runs
#          `git clean -xdf` in every west project — that last part is what
#          removes nuttx/build-<board>/, which `rm -rf build` would miss. It
#          therefore also deletes untracked+ignored files in every project, which
#          has two consequences: (a) don't point CI at a checkout you keep local
#          scratch work in; (b) it drops the in-tree downloaded tarballs the NuttX
#          build fetches (libcxx ~3.8MB, argtable3 ~0.5MB), so unlike the other
#          two SDKs this clean needs network. Preview any time with
#          `k230 bash -c "west clean -n"` — it has a real dry-run. If the
#          workspace is owned by a different user than the runner, git's
#          dubious-ownership check makes each per-project clean fail — and west
#          logs that but still exits 0, so only the zero-artifact assert catches
#          it. Fix with:
#          K230_CI_NUTTX_CLEAN_CMD="git config --global --add safe.directory '*'; west clean"
#          (the container HOME is ephemeral, so nothing leaks to the host).
#K230_CI_LINUX_CLEAN_CMD="rm -rf output"
#K230_CI_RTOS_CLEAN_CMD="make clean; rm -rf output"
#K230_CI_NUTTX_CLEAN_CMD="west clean"

# Local debugging escape hatch: skip every clean (t3's SDK cleans and t4's
# nncase-compiler dotnet prune) and let the builds be incremental. NEVER set this
# on the CI runner — it re-introduces exactly the vacuous pass the clean exists
# to prevent.
#K230_CI_NO_CLEAN=1

# Artifact glob asserted after each SDK build (find -name, newer than build
# start, >1MB) — and asserted to match NOTHING after the clean. Tighten per SDK
# if *.img is too loose; keep it consistent with the clean command.
#K230_CI_LINUX_ART=*.img
#K230_CI_RTOS_ART=*.img
#K230_CI_NUTTX_ART=*.img

# NuttX export sysroot dir (under the workspace, needs include/) for the
# nncase-runtime-nuttx stage; leave unset to skip that stage.
#K230_CI_NUTTX_EXPORT=nuttx-export

# Where reports/logs land (default: <repo>/reports, gitignored).
#K230_CI_REPORT_DIR=

# Per-stage wall-clock cap (any `timeout` duration). report.sh writes its report
# only after the whole stage loop, so without this a single hung stage blows the
# job-level timeout and the report is lost entirely. A capped stage just FAILs
# (exit 124, reported as TIMEOUT) and the report still gets written.
# regression.yml sets 4h; a value here overrides it.
#K230_CI_STAGE_TIMEOUT=4h
